   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Eigenvectors for good (multiplicity-1) weights\n\nA \"good\" weight (`FindGoodWeight2`) appears with multiplicity 1 in `rep1 ⊗ rep2`, so its weight\nsubspace is one-dimensional. The global Cartan generators `EMAll[j,j]` are already diagonal in\nthe GT tensor basis, so the corresponding Gaudin eigenvector is simply the *unique* joint\n`EMAll[j,j]` eigenvector with weight `repall` — no Hamiltonian solve is needed. This is exact and\ncostless at any dimension.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Shared weight-space primitive: joint spectrum of the global Cartans EMAll[j,j]\n   (diagonal in the GT tensor basis). Row i = weight of the i-th tensor basis state.\n   This is the pre-Tally body of the earlier FindWeight2 — kept as one named atom so the\n   weight-multiplicity tool and Psi both build on it instead of re-deriving it. *)\nClearAll[weightList, FindWeight2, Psi];\nweightList[rep1_, rep2_] := weightList[rep1, rep2] =\n   Transpose[Table[Diagonal[Normal[EMAll[j, j, rep1, rep2]]], {j, 4}]];\n\n(* general weight-multiplicity table (restored, now on top of weightList): {weight, mult}.\n   FindGoodWeight2 stays the fast Permutations[rep1+rep2] rectangular shortcut from above. *)\nFindWeight2[rep1_, rep2_] := Tally[weightList[rep1, rep2]];\n\n(* good weight => unique basis state; return it as the (unit) eigenvector.\n   $Failed[mult] if the weight is absent or not multiplicity-1 (i.e. not good). *)\nPsi[rep1_, rep2_, repall_] := Module[{pos = Position[weightList[rep1, rep2], repall]},\n   If[Length[pos] != 1, Return[$Failed[\"multiplicity=\" <> ToString[Length[pos]]]]];\n   SparseArray[{pos[[1, 1]] -> 1}, {dim[rep1] dim[rep2]}]];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* example: all good weights of {3,3,0,0}x{3,3,0,0} (2500-dim) -> unique basis states, instant.\n   'index' is the position of the nonzero component in the GT tensor basis. *)\nTable[{w, FirstPosition[Normal[Psi[{3,3,0,0},{3,3,0,0},w]], 1][[1]]}, {w, FindGoodWeight2[{3,3,0,0},{3,3,0,0}]}] // Column",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
